1
00:00:54,125 --> 00:00:58,166
He should be here somewhere.
That means he has landed on our side.

2
00:00:58,250 --> 00:00:59,583
Any update on the rescue chopper?

3
00:01:24,458 --> 00:01:25,291
Jai Hind.

4
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:40,000
The Indian Army
has spotted Ahuja's parachute.

5
00:01:40,083 --> 00:01:40,916
Where, sir?

6
00:01:42,458 --> 00:01:43,958
He's drifted across the LoC.

7
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:46,416
Ahuja is in PoK, Tony.

8
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,916
Dhali!

9
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,416
Ahuja ejected, man! Hurry up!

10
00:02:58,875 --> 00:03:00,208
This Ahuja…

11
00:03:00,291 --> 00:03:02,000
Always going overboard.

12
00:03:03,166 --> 00:03:04,166
No problem.

13
00:03:05,166 --> 00:03:06,875
Let's bring him back.

14
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:09,250
Sinha!

15
00:03:11,958 --> 00:03:14,000
Ahuja has ejected.
We have to go look for him.

16
00:03:14,083 --> 00:03:15,166
What? When?

17
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:16,583
Just a little while ago.

18
00:03:16,666 --> 00:03:18,958
We don't have much time.
Is there a chopper ready?

19
00:03:19,916 --> 00:03:21,708
-Is Nubra One ready at the takeoff point?
-Yes, sir.

20
00:03:21,791 --> 00:03:24,625
Run the final checks quickly.
I want to take off in two minutes.

21
00:03:25,416 --> 00:03:27,166
Did Ahuja activate his rescue beacon?

22
00:03:33,208 --> 00:03:35,625
Ahuja isn't in friendly territory, Sinha.

23
00:03:36,291 --> 00:03:37,791
I know him well.

24
00:03:37,875 --> 00:03:40,958
He will neither use the beacon
nor let them use it.

25
00:04:15,958 --> 00:04:17,958
Where the hell do you think you're going?

26
00:04:18,041 --> 00:04:19,708
We are going to get Ahuja, sir.

27
00:04:19,791 --> 00:04:21,458
Ahuja is in Pakistan, Tony.

28
00:04:21,541 --> 00:04:23,291
That doesn't matter, sir.

29
00:04:23,375 --> 00:04:25,833
Our choppers are fitted
with both guns and rockets.

30
00:04:25,916 --> 00:04:28,583
We will rescue him, sir.
You have to trust us.

31
00:04:28,666 --> 00:04:30,166
What if they shoot you?

32
00:04:30,916 --> 00:04:32,375
Who's going to go look for you?

33
00:04:34,125 --> 00:04:37,333
It's a trap. Basic military strategy.

34
00:04:37,416 --> 00:04:39,750
Sir, we can't just sit back
and do nothing.

35
00:04:44,291 --> 00:04:45,791
It is a diplomatic matter now.

36
00:04:45,875 --> 00:04:48,916
I'll talk to the government,
take it to the highest level.

37
00:04:50,041 --> 00:04:52,041
You cannot cross the LoC.

38
00:04:53,250 --> 00:04:54,541
Understood?

39
00:05:55,708 --> 00:05:57,958
In breaking news coming from South Asia,

40
00:05:58,041 --> 00:05:59,291
the Indian Air Force has confirmed

41
00:05:59,375 --> 00:06:02,083
that two of its fighter pilots
are missing in action

42
00:06:02,166 --> 00:06:04,166
after their jets were reportedly shot down

43
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:07,458
over the Line of Control
in Kashmir's Kargil sector.

44
00:06:07,541 --> 00:06:09,916
World leaders are monitoring
the developments closely

45
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,708
amidst widespread concern

46
00:06:11,791 --> 00:06:14,666
that this may prove to be
a dangerous tipping point

47
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:17,416
in the ongoing Kargil conflict
between the two…

48
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:18,708
Long live Pakistan, sir.

49
00:06:18,791 --> 00:06:20,166
I'm watching the news, Aziz.

50
00:06:20,250 --> 00:06:22,333
-Well done.
-Thank you, sir.

51
00:06:22,916 --> 00:06:26,666
But now this issue
will escalate internationally, Aziz.

52
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:30,375
American satellites
will be monitoring the Line of Control.

53
00:06:30,875 --> 00:06:32,083
So, for now,

54
00:06:32,166 --> 00:06:36,000
halt all movement of soldiers
and their supplies.

55
00:06:36,083 --> 00:06:39,666
Sir, India has deployed
15,000 more soldiers in the Kargil sector.

56
00:06:40,458 --> 00:06:41,625
Stopping the movement now--

57
00:06:41,708 --> 00:06:44,708
Whether it's 1,000 or 15,000,
what difference does it make, Aziz?

58
00:06:46,583 --> 00:06:49,333
It's been over three weeks
since we were discovered.

59
00:06:49,416 --> 00:06:51,458
We have killed 250 of their soldiers,

60
00:06:51,541 --> 00:06:52,791
shot down two jets.

61
00:06:52,875 --> 00:06:55,458
Has the Indian Air Force or the Army
managed to hurt us in any way?

62
00:06:55,541 --> 00:06:59,041
As long as we hold the height advantage,

63
00:06:59,125 --> 00:07:03,333
we'll keep crushing
both their Army and their Air Force.

64
00:07:05,041 --> 00:07:06,125
Right, sir.

65
00:07:06,208 --> 00:07:08,875
I trust both pilots are in our custody?

66
00:07:08,958 --> 00:07:10,708
We've caught one, sir.

67
00:07:10,791 --> 00:07:11,916
He's unconscious at the moment.

68
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,208
And the second?

69
00:07:13,291 --> 00:07:14,375
The search is ongoing, sir.

70
00:07:14,458 --> 00:07:16,500
The area has been identified.
We'll get him soon.

71
00:07:21,625 --> 00:07:22,666
Excellent.

72
00:07:24,208 --> 00:07:26,833
Let's see how many more pilots

73
00:07:26,916 --> 00:07:29,875
the Indian Air Force
is willing to send to their deaths.

74
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:00,750
We've found the parachute, sir.

75
00:08:05,833 --> 00:08:06,958
We've found the parachute, sir.

76
00:08:28,458 --> 00:08:29,958
The Station Commander himself is here.

77
00:08:34,250 --> 00:08:35,708
I hope it's nothing serious?

78
00:08:38,083 --> 00:08:40,500
No. He's not in ceremonial uniform.

79
00:08:40,583 --> 00:08:42,625
Ajay had to eject during a mission.

80
00:08:44,041 --> 00:08:46,125
We are waiting for further information.

81
00:08:46,208 --> 00:08:48,625
As soon as we find out more,
we'll update you.

82
00:10:11,791 --> 00:10:13,958
General Zinni, what a pleasant surprise.

83
00:10:14,041 --> 00:10:16,375
Is it, Mr. Prime Minister?

84
00:10:17,166 --> 00:10:21,250
My office has requested meetings
five times in the last week.

85
00:10:21,833 --> 00:10:23,541
I apologize, General.

86
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:27,125
The situation at the LoC is quite tense.

87
00:10:27,208 --> 00:10:29,458
Which is precisely why I'm calling.

88
00:10:30,291 --> 00:10:32,333
President Clinton is deeply concerned

89
00:10:32,416 --> 00:10:35,166
and wants you to de-escalate immediately.

90
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:37,041
They're not our troops, General.

91
00:10:37,833 --> 00:10:38,958
They are Mujahideen.

92
00:10:39,041 --> 00:10:42,625
Delhi claims that it's your army
disguised as militants.

93
00:10:42,708 --> 00:10:45,958
Quite frankly,
given the scale, it is compelling.

94
00:10:48,708 --> 00:10:50,458
Who do you trust, General?

95
00:10:51,166 --> 00:10:52,791
Your old ally, Pakistan,

96
00:10:53,666 --> 00:10:56,500
who stood by you faithfully
for the last 50 years--

97
00:10:56,583 --> 00:10:58,875
Speaking of allies, Mr. Prime Minister,

98
00:10:58,958 --> 00:11:01,416
what is your army chief doing in Beijing?

99
00:11:06,291 --> 00:11:10,000
That's a personal visit, General.
It has nothing to do with this situation.

100
00:11:10,083 --> 00:11:11,875
Mr. Sharif, you do understand

101
00:11:11,958 --> 00:11:14,833
that if India and Pakistan
go to nuclear war,

102
00:11:15,375 --> 00:11:19,416
100 million people could lose their lives
in the immediate aftermath?

103
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:20,833
Right now, sir,

104
00:11:20,916 --> 00:11:25,083
you are just one reckless decision away
from setting it off.

105
00:11:25,166 --> 00:11:27,875
President Clinton
is counting on your leadership,

106
00:11:28,458 --> 00:11:29,833
Mr. Prime Minister.

107
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:37,416
This is my third war.

108
00:11:41,666 --> 00:11:43,125
And today…

109
00:11:44,750 --> 00:11:47,833
may well be the most difficult day…

110
00:11:49,166 --> 00:11:50,125
of my entire career.

111
00:11:57,083 --> 00:12:00,250
With great regret,

112
00:12:00,875 --> 00:12:05,958
I am suspending Operation Safed Sagar.

113
00:12:13,666 --> 00:12:14,916
With due respect, sir,

114
00:12:15,458 --> 00:12:17,333
we were first ordered

115
00:12:17,416 --> 00:12:19,833
not to cross the LoC
while engaging the enemy.

116
00:12:19,916 --> 00:12:21,500
We didn't cross it.

117
00:12:22,083 --> 00:12:25,750
Then we were told
not to cross the LoC even to rescue Ahuja.

118
00:12:26,708 --> 00:12:28,083
We didn't cross it then either.

119
00:12:28,166 --> 00:12:31,000
But now we're being told not to fight
even from our side of the LoC?

120
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:32,208
How can this be, sir?

121
00:12:32,291 --> 00:12:36,708
Tony, we have to face the hard facts.

122
00:12:37,208 --> 00:12:40,500
In the last two days,
we have lost two aircraft and two pilots.

123
00:12:40,583 --> 00:12:43,000
We can't go down without a fight, sir.

124
00:12:43,083 --> 00:12:44,916
Sir, I agree with Tony.

125
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,000
We have to keep fighting.

126
00:12:46,083 --> 00:12:48,666
You're all missing the big picture here.

127
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:55,000
This is the Western Air Command's
area of responsibility.

128
00:12:55,083 --> 00:12:58,458
From Rajasthan to Jammu and Kashmir.

129
00:12:58,541 --> 00:13:01,166
The area spans 3.5 lakh square kilometers.

130
00:13:01,250 --> 00:13:02,750
On this map,

131
00:13:02,833 --> 00:13:05,500
Kargil is just a tiny dot.

132
00:13:05,583 --> 00:13:08,041
If losses continue at this rate,

133
00:13:08,125 --> 00:13:11,916
then within a month,
in an attempt to protect this tiny dot,

134
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,458
the entire Western Air Command
will be engaged.

135
00:13:15,041 --> 00:13:17,291
And if the enemy opens another front,

136
00:13:17,375 --> 00:13:19,791
how will we protect
the rest of these borders?

137
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,916
Tony, I'm angry, too.

138
00:13:28,250 --> 00:13:30,583
But we work on cold strategy.

139
00:13:30,666 --> 00:13:32,125
We will strike,

140
00:13:32,208 --> 00:13:34,708
but from outside missile range.

141
00:13:35,708 --> 00:13:36,541
But, sir,

142
00:13:37,083 --> 00:13:38,750
that's 10,000 feet above the target.

143
00:13:38,833 --> 00:13:42,041
If we can't achieve precision
even from this close,

144
00:13:42,125 --> 00:13:43,458
how will we from that height?

145
00:13:43,541 --> 00:13:46,083
That's exactly why we are going to wait.

146
00:13:46,583 --> 00:13:48,750
The target is at 18,000 feet.

147
00:13:48,833 --> 00:13:51,333
Bombing needs to be done from 30,000 feet.

148
00:13:51,416 --> 00:13:55,625
And only an advanced aircraft
like the Mirage can do this.

149
00:13:55,708 --> 00:14:01,875
Because only the Mirage 2000 has
laser-guided bombing capability,

150
00:14:01,958 --> 00:14:06,083
which can lock onto targets from far away
from the peak,

151
00:14:06,166 --> 00:14:07,916
beyond missile range.

152
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:12,041
And it can strike before
the enemy can react

153
00:14:12,125 --> 00:14:14,083
and safely return.

154
00:14:14,166 --> 00:14:17,291
But unfortunately,
they're not ready yet either,

155
00:14:17,375 --> 00:14:20,750
because they don't have
laser-guided bombs.

156
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:26,375
The Americans have once again rejected
our request for laser-guided bombs.

157
00:14:27,291 --> 00:14:29,750
It's clear America is playing with us.

158
00:14:29,833 --> 00:14:32,375
We have the capabilities,
but not the equipment.

159
00:14:32,458 --> 00:14:34,916
So we'll make our own laser-guided bombs,

160
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,833
and showcase the innovative capabilities
of the Indian Air Force to the world.

161
00:14:38,916 --> 00:14:41,833
We have old bombs from 1971.

162
00:14:41,916 --> 00:14:44,083
We'll fit these Paveway laser kits to them

163
00:14:44,833 --> 00:14:46,833
and lead this Mirage 2000 into believing

164
00:14:46,916 --> 00:14:48,666
that they're laser-guided bombs.

165
00:14:48,750 --> 00:14:51,041
Until the jet accepts this hack,

166
00:14:51,125 --> 00:14:52,333
nobody goes home.

167
00:14:52,958 --> 00:14:54,250
At any cost…

168
00:14:56,625 --> 00:14:58,125
we need to fool this jet.

169
00:15:04,666 --> 00:15:05,500
Sangy sir,

170
00:15:06,166 --> 00:15:07,833
there's a call for you from Srinagar.

171
00:15:11,791 --> 00:15:12,666
Hello?

172
00:15:12,750 --> 00:15:13,666
Sangy,

173
00:15:14,208 --> 00:15:15,458
it's Baldy.

174
00:15:15,541 --> 00:15:16,500
Baldy?

175
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:18,875
How are you?

176
00:15:19,791 --> 00:15:20,875
Any news of Ahuja sir?

177
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:25,166
There's no news.

178
00:15:25,708 --> 00:15:27,916
Our operations have also been halted.

179
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,500
Yes, Chhabra sir told me.

180
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,833
Tell me something.

181
00:15:32,583 --> 00:15:34,333
What's happening with the Mirages?

182
00:15:34,416 --> 00:15:36,041
When do you think you'll be operational?

183
00:15:36,125 --> 00:15:37,708
We are trying our best.

184
00:15:37,791 --> 00:15:39,541
Everyone's working around the clock.

185
00:15:40,875 --> 00:15:41,708
Listen, Baldy,

186
00:15:43,666 --> 00:15:45,041
how's Dhali?

187
00:15:46,208 --> 00:15:47,708
He was with Ahuja sir, wasn't he?

188
00:15:49,208 --> 00:15:51,416
Ever since he came back,
he's barely spoken to anyone.

189
00:15:52,666 --> 00:15:54,208
Maybe he is blaming himself.

190
00:15:56,041 --> 00:15:59,041
We're all just hoping
that wherever Ahuja sir is,

191
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:00,500
he comes back safe.

192
00:16:01,916 --> 00:16:05,708
Nothing should happen
to either of our pilots.

193
00:16:05,791 --> 00:16:08,583
Jaswant ji, please send
a message to Islamabad.

194
00:16:08,666 --> 00:16:11,375
They should be treated properly.

195
00:16:11,458 --> 00:16:12,458
Otherwise,

196
00:16:12,541 --> 00:16:15,375
the outcome will be grave for Pakistan.

197
00:16:16,583 --> 00:16:17,416
Yes.

198
00:16:27,333 --> 00:16:28,208
Get him down.

199
00:16:30,125 --> 00:16:30,958
Get down.

200
00:16:43,166 --> 00:16:44,791
Well done, Ajmal.

201
00:16:45,291 --> 00:16:46,791
You know what you have to do.

202
00:16:47,625 --> 00:16:48,541
Yes, sir.

203
00:16:49,250 --> 00:16:50,083
Move.

204
00:17:05,666 --> 00:17:07,500
Squadron Leader Ajay Ahuja,

205
00:17:08,375 --> 00:17:10,541
what were you doing so close to the LoC?

206
00:17:11,750 --> 00:17:13,041
What was your objective?

207
00:17:15,416 --> 00:17:18,041
Under the Geneva Conventions of 1949,

208
00:17:18,958 --> 00:17:20,750
prisoners of war

209
00:17:20,833 --> 00:17:23,375
are not mandated to answer questions
posed by the enemy.

210
00:17:23,458 --> 00:17:24,291
Speak up!

211
00:17:35,708 --> 00:17:38,166
Answer the question directly.

212
00:17:38,708 --> 00:17:40,375
Why are you here?

213
00:17:40,458 --> 00:17:41,833
Perhaps, you should first ask yourself…

214
00:17:44,958 --> 00:17:46,291
You…

215
00:17:48,458 --> 00:17:49,875
Why did you come inside my country?

216
00:17:57,416 --> 00:17:59,916
With India maintaining
that both jets were shot down

217
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,958
on their side of the Line of Control,

218
00:18:02,041 --> 00:18:06,625
the fog of war in Kargil has now thickened
into a global diplomatic crisis.

219
00:18:06,708 --> 00:18:07,958
Speaking earlier today,

220
00:18:08,041 --> 00:18:11,208
the US Secretary of State
urged maximum restraint,

221
00:18:11,291 --> 00:18:14,791
reminding the world that a nuclear
exchange between India and Pakistan

222
00:18:14,875 --> 00:18:17,250
-could result in a hundred million deaths…
-Aziz.

223
00:18:17,333 --> 00:18:19,791
-…in the immediate aftermath.
-Is the other pilot in our custody?

224
00:18:19,875 --> 00:18:21,791
Yes, sir. He's been taken to Skardu.

225
00:18:22,416 --> 00:18:24,791
And has he agreed to accept the truth?

226
00:18:26,083 --> 00:18:28,333
Sorry, sir, I don't understand.

227
00:18:28,416 --> 00:18:30,958
That he was ordered
to cross the Line of Control

228
00:18:31,041 --> 00:18:34,625
and bomb our forward bases.

229
00:18:34,708 --> 00:18:38,375
It's very important to get
this on-camera statement from him, Aziz.

230
00:18:38,458 --> 00:18:40,541
So that we can mislead the world

231
00:18:40,625 --> 00:18:43,250
into thinking that
the real aggressor is India, not us.

232
00:18:43,333 --> 00:18:45,333
I'll check, sir.

233
00:18:46,541 --> 00:18:48,625
But General Hassan tells me

234
00:18:48,708 --> 00:18:51,541
the officer is extremely stubborn.

235
00:18:51,625 --> 00:18:55,666
General Hassan isn't capable
of handling every situation.

236
00:18:56,375 --> 00:18:57,416
You see to it yourself.

237
00:18:57,500 --> 00:18:59,416
Copy that, sir. Understood.

238
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:01,375
I'll leave for Skardu immediately.

239
00:19:03,791 --> 00:19:05,000
I am asking once again.

240
00:19:05,083 --> 00:19:08,166
Which base were you ordered
to bomb inside Pakistan?

241
00:19:09,875 --> 00:19:11,500
I am telling you again.

242
00:19:14,916 --> 00:19:17,208
There were no bombs in my aircraft.

243
00:19:18,250 --> 00:19:20,000
And I also didn't…

244
00:19:20,541 --> 00:19:22,375
intend to enter Pakistan.

245
00:19:22,458 --> 00:19:23,291
Lies!

246
00:19:23,375 --> 00:19:24,666
Absolute lies.

247
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:26,500
Which base?

248
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:28,750
Which base?

249
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:38,291
Which base?

250
00:19:39,416 --> 00:19:41,000
Major Ajmal!

251
00:19:41,083 --> 00:19:42,708
-Which base?
-Major Ajmal!

252
00:19:45,208 --> 00:19:46,041
What's going on here?

253
00:19:52,166 --> 00:19:53,166
Untie the rope.

254
00:19:53,791 --> 00:19:54,708
Put his uniform back on.

255
00:19:56,458 --> 00:19:57,583
And you.

256
00:19:57,666 --> 00:19:58,958
Fetch Dr. Bukhari.

257
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:10,375
What are you doing, Hassan?

258
00:20:10,458 --> 00:20:12,083
This is Skardu, sir.

259
00:20:12,958 --> 00:20:14,916
This is how we extract information here.

260
00:20:16,041 --> 00:20:18,000
Hassan, this is different.

261
00:20:18,541 --> 00:20:20,666
Do you have any idea

262
00:20:20,750 --> 00:20:22,416
how important his statement is?

263
00:20:26,666 --> 00:20:28,833
I apologize for Major Ajmal's conduct.

264
00:20:29,666 --> 00:20:31,458
But you are very stubborn.

265
00:20:31,541 --> 00:20:33,583
And our soldiers…

266
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:36,541
respond to stubbornness

267
00:20:36,625 --> 00:20:37,666
in this fashion.

268
00:20:38,458 --> 00:20:39,541
Now, what can one do?

269
00:20:40,541 --> 00:20:42,125
You can, General Khan.

270
00:20:44,666 --> 00:20:46,166
You can give them good training.

271
00:20:47,125 --> 00:20:48,250
So that they know

272
00:20:48,333 --> 00:20:51,541
that any form of torture
meted out to a prisoner of war

273
00:20:51,625 --> 00:20:53,416
is a violation of the Geneva Conventions.

274
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:55,041
What Geneva Conventions?

275
00:20:56,291 --> 00:20:59,375
They apply only when
the armies of two nations

276
00:20:59,458 --> 00:21:00,708
are at war with each other.

277
00:21:01,916 --> 00:21:03,750
Those people who have entered Kargil,

278
00:21:04,458 --> 00:21:07,041
in response to which
you have entered our territory,

279
00:21:07,125 --> 00:21:08,416
are Mujahideen.

280
00:21:10,541 --> 00:21:12,458
I'm sorry, General Khan, I didn't know

281
00:21:13,375 --> 00:21:15,541
that by merely wearing a Pathani suit,

282
00:21:16,166 --> 00:21:18,083
Pakistan's army becomes Mujahideen.

283
00:21:26,333 --> 00:21:28,416
Aren't you worried about Ankur and Alka?

284
00:21:34,250 --> 00:21:35,625
Sir, you don't need to worry about them.

285
00:21:36,541 --> 00:21:38,708
They are in the safest place in India.

286
00:21:38,791 --> 00:21:40,125
And you're here,

287
00:21:40,833 --> 00:21:44,166
in Pakistan's most secure army base.

288
00:21:44,833 --> 00:21:46,375
No one will come here to save you.

289
00:21:49,125 --> 00:21:50,083
Here, only…

290
00:21:51,250 --> 00:21:52,708
I can help you.

291
00:21:55,250 --> 00:21:56,708
For that,

292
00:21:57,708 --> 00:21:59,875
you have to help me first.

293
00:22:19,916 --> 00:22:21,083
Please have some tea.

294
00:22:41,041 --> 00:22:42,041
General Musharraf,

295
00:22:42,708 --> 00:22:45,791
Beijing welcomes you
during difficult times.

296
00:22:45,875 --> 00:22:47,833
-Thank you.
-Please, sit.

297
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:55,250
My deepest sympathies
regarding your embassy in Belgrade.

298
00:22:56,250 --> 00:22:57,791
Three journalists dead.

299
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:00,791
"American mistake," they claim.

300
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:03,458
We have a saying in Urdu.

301
00:23:10,541 --> 00:23:12,541
"Their own roof is falling apart,

302
00:23:12,625 --> 00:23:15,708
but they are off
to repair others' houses."

303
00:23:16,666 --> 00:23:18,583
And this is what America is doing.

304
00:23:19,375 --> 00:23:20,666
For the last few weeks,

305
00:23:20,750 --> 00:23:24,875
India has been displaying unrestrained
aggression along the Line of Control.

306
00:23:24,958 --> 00:23:26,000
And yet,

307
00:23:26,625 --> 00:23:30,541
my prime minister is receiving
daily calls from Clinton.

308
00:23:31,166 --> 00:23:32,166
What should we do?

309
00:23:32,250 --> 00:23:35,416
Should we sit back and allow India
to take over our country?

310
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:39,333
America is acting through India. Trust me.

311
00:23:40,208 --> 00:23:42,333
We can easily take on India.

312
00:23:43,375 --> 00:23:44,291
But America?

313
00:23:47,333 --> 00:23:48,208
General,

314
00:23:49,708 --> 00:23:51,416
we also have a saying in Mandarin.

315
00:23:58,208 --> 00:24:03,083
"A frog at the bottom of the well
cannot fathom the depth of the ocean."

316
00:24:05,708 --> 00:24:09,708
It is a very stupid thing,
what you've done in Kargil, General.

317
00:24:10,708 --> 00:24:14,333
Sparking war in the midst
of a historic peace process,

318
00:24:14,416 --> 00:24:17,041
while both sides have nuclear weapons.

319
00:24:17,125 --> 00:24:18,500
You're playing with fire.

320
00:24:19,166 --> 00:24:21,958
China has always
supported Pakistan in the past.

321
00:24:22,041 --> 00:24:22,875
But this time,

322
00:24:23,458 --> 00:24:24,625
you're on your own.

323
00:24:47,333 --> 00:24:50,166
Your safety has sparked concern
not just in India,

324
00:24:50,250 --> 00:24:52,125
but across the world as well.

325
00:24:53,583 --> 00:24:54,458
So,

326
00:24:56,666 --> 00:24:59,416
we will record a video of you.

327
00:25:01,291 --> 00:25:05,416
We got this written in Hindustani for you.

328
00:25:06,208 --> 00:25:08,041
All you have to do
is look into the camera,

329
00:25:08,125 --> 00:25:10,750
and read whatever
is written on it properly.

330
00:25:10,833 --> 00:25:12,625
So, let's get started?

331
00:25:22,625 --> 00:25:23,458
Zubair.

332
00:25:28,333 --> 00:25:29,916
"I, Squadron Leader Ajay Ahuja,

333
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:33,250
am making this statement
of my own free will and in my senses."

334
00:25:34,541 --> 00:25:37,083
"Today, on May 27, 1999,

335
00:25:37,708 --> 00:25:38,541
when I…"

336
00:25:39,416 --> 00:25:42,250
WHEN I WAS ATTEMPTING AN ATTACK
ON A PAKISTANI MILITARY BASE

337
00:25:45,750 --> 00:25:50,166
While I was engaged in a non-offensive
mission within Indian territory,

338
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:53,500
then the Pakistani Army
that has infiltrated Kargil…

339
00:25:57,541 --> 00:25:59,625
-What happened, sir?
-Don't they teach you to read over there?

340
00:25:59,708 --> 00:26:01,125
They do, sir.

341
00:26:02,500 --> 00:26:04,500
How to read and how to fight, too.

342
00:26:05,333 --> 00:26:06,416
But with principles.

343
00:26:08,166 --> 00:26:10,041
What do they teach you
this side of the border, sir?

344
00:26:18,958 --> 00:26:20,333
So, according to you,

345
00:26:21,541 --> 00:26:24,625
your mission was limited
to Indian airspace only.

346
00:26:25,791 --> 00:26:27,375
Then would you care to explain

347
00:26:27,458 --> 00:26:28,708
what you're doing

348
00:26:29,708 --> 00:26:31,583
at a Pakistan Army base right now?

349
00:26:33,166 --> 00:26:37,416
Sir, the Pakistan Army
hidden in our mountains

350
00:26:38,166 --> 00:26:40,875
fired a Stinger missile at my jet.

351
00:26:42,708 --> 00:26:44,083
I ejected…

352
00:26:45,083 --> 00:26:46,083
in India.

353
00:26:46,833 --> 00:26:48,958
My parachute carried me into Pakistan.

354
00:26:51,625 --> 00:26:52,625
So,

355
00:26:53,625 --> 00:26:55,416
entering Pakistan…

356
00:26:56,416 --> 00:26:57,625
was never your intention?

357
00:26:58,541 --> 00:26:59,958
Affirmative, sir.

358
00:27:00,041 --> 00:27:01,291
Very well. Let's talk straight.

359
00:27:01,875 --> 00:27:03,333
Tell one lie for us.

360
00:27:03,416 --> 00:27:04,541
Then, inshallah,

361
00:27:05,291 --> 00:27:07,333
go back and collect
your medal for bravery.

362
00:27:09,541 --> 00:27:11,625
Which country awards medals for lying?

363
00:27:13,500 --> 00:27:16,208
And anyway, no medal is valuable enough…

364
00:27:17,625 --> 00:27:19,333
for me to betray my country.

365
00:27:25,166 --> 00:27:27,125
You also have another option.

366
00:27:28,250 --> 00:27:30,166
We will shift you to London.

367
00:27:30,250 --> 00:27:32,000
You'll get so much…

368
00:27:33,083 --> 00:27:35,333
that you won't need a medal…

369
00:27:35,833 --> 00:27:37,041
or your uniform.

370
00:27:39,250 --> 00:27:41,375
There's something special, sir,
about this uniform.

371
00:27:44,250 --> 00:27:47,833
It's not like any passerby
can buy it off the street and wear it.

372
00:27:52,000 --> 00:27:55,041
To wear it,
you have to pledge your life to India.

373
00:27:58,500 --> 00:27:59,416
Anyway,

374
00:27:59,500 --> 00:28:02,041
I have told you everything
I'm supposed to tell you.

375
00:28:03,875 --> 00:28:05,666
You're a three-star general.

376
00:28:06,416 --> 00:28:08,666
Your time is very valuable.

377
00:28:08,750 --> 00:28:10,458
Don't waste it on me.

378
00:28:12,416 --> 00:28:13,416
Jai Hind, sir.

379
00:28:18,791 --> 00:28:22,708
He who cannot understand the difference
between principles and madness…

380
00:28:25,458 --> 00:28:26,708
neither I…

381
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:29,416
nor God can save him.

382
00:28:37,250 --> 00:28:38,750
Aziz, what's the update?

383
00:28:38,833 --> 00:28:40,916
Sir, I tried everything,

384
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,583
but he's very stubborn, sir.

385
00:28:42,666 --> 00:28:44,583
If he is stubborn,
then make an example of him.

386
00:28:45,541 --> 00:28:46,916
Do you know what I mean?

387
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,750
Sir, but the international community?

388
00:28:48,833 --> 00:28:50,666
Screw the international community.

389
00:28:51,333 --> 00:28:55,833
Make such an example of him that before
they even think of entering Pakistan,

390
00:28:55,916 --> 00:28:57,500
their blood runs cold.

391
00:28:57,583 --> 00:28:58,458
Sir.

392
00:29:51,708 --> 00:29:53,958
Jai Hind.

393
00:31:00,208 --> 00:31:02,250
"Compound fracture of the leg tibia.

394
00:31:02,333 --> 00:31:05,291
Multiple gunshot wounds
to the thoracic cavity and cranium.

395
00:31:05,375 --> 00:31:06,333
Extensive…

396
00:31:08,916 --> 00:31:12,833
cigarette-induced burn injuries across
the abdominal region and genitalia."

397
00:31:12,916 --> 00:31:15,375
Signs of deliberate mutilation,
including broken fingers--"

398
00:31:15,458 --> 00:31:17,208
Everything is visible, Doctor.

399
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:20,041
I can see it.

400
00:31:21,583 --> 00:31:23,291
All that they've done to him.

401
00:31:31,458 --> 00:31:34,041
Can we take the body?

402
00:31:34,625 --> 00:31:35,708
Yes, sir.

403
00:31:35,791 --> 00:31:36,833
But there is a problem.

404
00:31:37,333 --> 00:31:38,291
What's the problem?

405
00:31:39,916 --> 00:31:43,208
The coffin Pakistan sent his body in
is a foot and a half too short.

406
00:31:43,291 --> 00:31:45,250
And inside that only, they have…

407
00:31:48,625 --> 00:31:49,625
So, all this?

408
00:31:50,625 --> 00:31:52,791
-Who'll arrange all of this?
-I'll arrange it, sir.

409
00:32:02,666 --> 00:32:05,875
The situation in the Kargil War
is becoming increasingly grave.

410
00:32:05,958 --> 00:32:09,291
Today, even a joint operation
of the Indian Army and Air Force

411
00:32:09,375 --> 00:32:12,666
failed to recapture the Tololing Complex.

412
00:32:12,750 --> 00:32:15,458
In this effort, both forces
have suffered heavy setbacks.

413
00:32:15,541 --> 00:32:18,791
The intruders,
using surface-to-air missiles,

414
00:32:18,875 --> 00:32:22,958
targeted Mi-17 attack helicopters
of the Indian Air Force.

415
00:32:24,250 --> 00:32:25,541
In just two days,

416
00:32:25,625 --> 00:32:28,458
this is the third Air Force aircraft
that has been shot down.

417
00:32:28,541 --> 00:32:31,083
In this incident,
Squadron Leader Rajiv Pundir,

418
00:32:31,166 --> 00:32:33,375
Flight Lieutenant Subramaniam Muhilan,

419
00:32:33,458 --> 00:32:37,083
Sergeant PVNR Prasad,
and Sergeant Raj Kishore Sahu

420
00:32:37,166 --> 00:32:39,166
have attained martyrdom.

421
00:32:39,250 --> 00:32:43,541
Earlier, after shooting down
Squadron Leader Ajay Ahuja's MiG-21,

422
00:32:43,625 --> 00:32:45,208
the Pakistani Army
had subjected him to brutal torture.

423
00:32:45,291 --> 00:32:46,708
WAKE UP, PAKISTAN,
OR BECOME A GRAVEYARD!

424
00:32:48,416 --> 00:32:50,791
There is widespread outrage across India,

425
00:32:50,875 --> 00:32:52,000
even as Pakistan claims

426
00:32:52,083 --> 00:32:56,541
that Squadron Leader Ajay Ahuja died
from injuries sustained during ejection.

427
00:32:56,625 --> 00:32:58,791
Squadron Leader Ahuja

428
00:32:58,875 --> 00:33:01,250
unfortunately had been killed
in the accident.

429
00:33:01,333 --> 00:33:05,416
India has formally accused Pakistan
of violating the Geneva Conventions.

430
00:33:05,500 --> 00:33:07,708
The killing of a downed pilot,
if confirmed,

431
00:33:07,791 --> 00:33:10,416
would constitute a grave breach
of international law.

432
00:33:10,500 --> 00:33:13,666
This is a cold-blooded murder,
an act of cowardice,

433
00:33:13,750 --> 00:33:15,500
on the part of Pakistani regulars.

434
00:33:22,750 --> 00:33:25,333
General Aziz, why didn't you tell us

435
00:33:25,416 --> 00:33:28,541
that the Indian fighter pilot
was tortured to death?

436
00:33:29,208 --> 00:33:31,500
Sir, our official stance
is absolutely clear.

437
00:33:32,208 --> 00:33:34,375
Squadron Leader Ajay Ahuja

438
00:33:34,458 --> 00:33:36,250
died due to the ejection impact.

439
00:33:36,333 --> 00:33:38,333
India is blaming us,

440
00:33:38,416 --> 00:33:40,791
saying we are violating
the Geneva Conventions.

441
00:33:41,583 --> 00:33:43,750
America is checking in with me daily,

442
00:33:43,833 --> 00:33:45,166
pressurizing us

443
00:33:45,250 --> 00:33:47,333
to release the other pilot immediately.

444
00:33:47,916 --> 00:33:48,958
Aziz sahib,

445
00:33:49,041 --> 00:33:50,375
immediately start the process

446
00:33:50,458 --> 00:33:52,875
of handing over that pilot to India.

447
00:33:53,833 --> 00:33:54,916
Long live Pakistan.

448
00:33:55,500 --> 00:33:56,833
General Musharraf?

449
00:33:57,791 --> 00:33:59,583
Did you come straight from the airport?

450
00:34:09,375 --> 00:34:13,041
I thought I shouldn't delay too much
in delivering the good news, Sharif sahib.

451
00:34:14,583 --> 00:34:18,708
China has congratulated us
on giving India a bloody nose.

452
00:34:18,791 --> 00:34:21,541
China is with us, Mian sahib.

453
00:34:22,125 --> 00:34:25,500
And if America
still pressures us to withdraw,

454
00:34:25,583 --> 00:34:27,875
we can count on China.

455
00:34:27,958 --> 00:34:29,833
That's wonderful news.

456
00:34:29,916 --> 00:34:32,666
Meaning, we don't need America anymore?

457
00:34:32,750 --> 00:34:33,958
That's right.

458
00:34:35,208 --> 00:34:36,416
Sartaj sahib,

459
00:34:37,833 --> 00:34:40,000
you and Nawaz sahib
keep the Americans occupied.

460
00:34:41,916 --> 00:34:43,541
It's time…

461
00:34:46,291 --> 00:34:48,500
we deal with Delhi directly.

462
00:36:46,416 --> 00:36:48,375
You were the one I trusted,

463
00:36:49,750 --> 00:36:50,708
Tony.

464
00:36:54,916 --> 00:36:56,875
Why did you let him go there?

465
00:36:59,916 --> 00:37:01,041
Why?

466
00:37:59,375 --> 00:38:00,333
Fire!

467
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:04,833
Fire!

468
00:38:17,583 --> 00:38:24,541
BHISIANA CREMATORIUM

469
00:38:38,541 --> 00:38:39,916
Sir, before the war of '71,

470
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:42,958
there was an explosion
caused by someone else's safety lapse.

471
00:38:44,291 --> 00:38:46,625
My father had shrapnel lodged in his body.

472
00:38:49,166 --> 00:38:50,708
Even surgery could not remove them.

473
00:38:51,583 --> 00:38:53,541
After a few years, he left us.

474
00:39:00,166 --> 00:39:02,333
And today, we lost Ahuja sir.

475
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:05,083
He was like a father to me, sir.

476
00:39:12,083 --> 00:39:14,166
I'm really very sorry, Sangy.

477
00:39:14,833 --> 00:39:16,583
I have to fly in this war, sir.

478
00:39:19,916 --> 00:39:21,083
I have to fly.

479
00:39:24,708 --> 00:39:26,333
I have to go back to Golden Arrows.

480
00:39:27,166 --> 00:39:28,458
To my family.

481
00:40:12,916 --> 00:40:14,666
They killed him, Kamal.

482
00:40:20,916 --> 00:40:22,333
They tortured him.

483
00:40:34,166 --> 00:40:37,208
The bastards shot him point-blank.

484
00:40:40,166 --> 00:40:41,875
And they're saying that

485
00:40:42,375 --> 00:40:44,625
he died from ejection impact.

486
00:40:47,541 --> 00:40:52,250
They're lying, and here we are
sitting with our operation on hold.

487
00:40:55,541 --> 00:40:57,333
Tony, it's not your fault.

488
00:41:00,041 --> 00:41:01,708
I called him here.

489
00:41:03,250 --> 00:41:04,625
I called him here!

490
00:41:06,541 --> 00:41:08,958
This was not his regular posting.

491
00:41:13,458 --> 00:41:16,083
"Ahuja, come." He came, and…

492
00:41:44,708 --> 00:41:45,708
Hello?

493
00:41:45,791 --> 00:41:48,291
Sir, Wing Commander Sandeep Chhabra
is on the line from Gwalior.

494
00:41:48,375 --> 00:41:49,208
Connect.

495
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:50,958
Sandy.

496
00:41:53,125 --> 00:41:54,458
I'm very sorry, Tony.

497
00:41:56,250 --> 00:41:58,791
I know Ahuja was special.

498
00:41:59,291 --> 00:42:01,333
Sorry won't do, Sandy.

499
00:42:02,791 --> 00:42:05,208
We have to bomb them to Dark Ages.

500
00:42:05,291 --> 00:42:07,000
We're boiling inside, too, Tony.

501
00:42:07,541 --> 00:42:10,250
But we can't fly the Mirages
until trials are done.

502
00:42:10,750 --> 00:42:11,916
Won't get clearance.

503
00:42:12,625 --> 00:42:14,416
How much longer
are your trials going to take?

504
00:42:14,500 --> 00:42:15,791
I don't know, man.

505
00:42:16,625 --> 00:42:18,125
French plane, Israeli laser kit,

506
00:42:18,208 --> 00:42:20,083
old Indian bombs from 1971.

507
00:42:20,666 --> 00:42:21,958
Hacking all this together

508
00:42:22,041 --> 00:42:24,166
and making it work is a tricky setup.

509
00:42:24,750 --> 00:42:26,083
But we are trying.

510
00:42:27,500 --> 00:42:28,333
We're trying, Tony.

511
00:42:29,791 --> 00:42:30,833
Well, listen,

512
00:42:30,916 --> 00:42:32,250
Sangy wants to come back to you.

513
00:42:32,333 --> 00:42:33,875
He is emotional.

514
00:42:34,708 --> 00:42:36,208
But I'm okay with it.

515
00:42:36,291 --> 00:42:38,125
What's he going to do
even if he comes here?

516
00:42:38,208 --> 00:42:40,750
The entire operation
has been suspended here.

517
00:42:43,666 --> 00:42:45,541
How strange, isn't it, Sandy?

518
00:42:47,375 --> 00:42:49,958
You can bomb outside missile range,

519
00:42:50,041 --> 00:42:51,916
but you don't have bombs.

520
00:42:53,208 --> 00:42:55,041
The MiG-27 has bombs,

521
00:42:55,125 --> 00:42:58,083
but they cannot bomb
from outside missile range.

522
00:42:59,166 --> 00:43:01,916
We have GPS,
we can get close to the target,

523
00:43:02,000 --> 00:43:03,000
but bombing…

524
00:43:09,916 --> 00:43:11,208
Tony? Hello?

525
00:43:12,166 --> 00:43:13,083
Are you there?

526
00:43:14,333 --> 00:43:16,541
Sandy, I'll… I'll call you back.

527
00:43:17,250 --> 00:43:18,333
I'll call you back.

528
00:43:27,625 --> 00:43:28,458
We…

529
00:43:29,875 --> 00:43:32,083
don't need to halt the operation.

530
00:43:33,083 --> 00:43:33,958
Meaning?

531
00:43:34,458 --> 00:43:35,416
Kamal, we…

532
00:43:36,125 --> 00:43:38,583
We can bomb, but…

533
00:43:38,666 --> 00:43:39,500
But?

534
00:43:41,625 --> 00:43:42,875
But what?

535
00:43:44,458 --> 00:43:45,916
I will not get permission.

536
00:43:47,916 --> 00:43:48,875
Permission?

537
00:43:51,791 --> 00:43:53,791
Did they ask for permission

538
00:43:53,875 --> 00:43:55,583
before entering our country?

539
00:43:59,625 --> 00:44:02,041
Did they ask for permission
before torturing Ahuja?

540
00:44:09,708 --> 00:44:10,708
Sardar,

541
00:44:11,916 --> 00:44:13,583
do whatever you want to do,

542
00:44:14,875 --> 00:44:16,375
however you want to do it.

543
00:44:19,791 --> 00:44:20,833
Just do it.

544
00:44:23,500 --> 00:44:27,083
They think sitting up there at that
altitude, they can do what they want.

545
00:44:28,208 --> 00:44:29,458
They are wrong.

546
00:44:30,625 --> 00:44:32,458
We will mourn no more.

547
00:44:37,500 --> 00:44:39,916
We won't take any more photos either.

548
00:44:43,041 --> 00:44:44,333
Our jets

549
00:44:44,416 --> 00:44:46,375
have cameras installed in place of bombs.

550
00:44:47,500 --> 00:44:49,708
But the place is for bombs, isn't it?

551
00:44:50,708 --> 00:44:53,750
Now, we will bomb.

552
00:44:55,708 --> 00:44:57,416
We have GPS.

553
00:44:57,958 --> 00:44:59,958
We can fly above the clouds

554
00:45:00,041 --> 00:45:01,708
to reach our target.

555
00:45:03,291 --> 00:45:05,375
And staying outside their missile range,

556
00:45:05,458 --> 00:45:07,625
we can rain fire on them.

557
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:10,666
It's never been done before.

558
00:45:10,750 --> 00:45:12,333
But we'll do it.

559
00:45:15,583 --> 00:45:17,458
-Are you with me?
-Yes, sir!

560
00:45:22,166 --> 00:45:24,958
Tony, when was the last time
a photo-recce squadron

561
00:45:25,041 --> 00:45:26,541
took on the role of a bombing squadron?

562
00:45:26,625 --> 00:45:28,416
That too in the middle of a war.

563
00:45:29,791 --> 00:45:32,500
Sir, when was the last time
any air force in the world

564
00:45:32,583 --> 00:45:34,458
fought a war at 18,000 feet?

565
00:45:35,250 --> 00:45:36,458
My objection is purely technical.

566
00:45:36,541 --> 00:45:40,125
MiGs are designed
to drop bombs from 20,000 feet.

567
00:45:40,208 --> 00:45:41,666
Not from 30,000 feet.

568
00:45:41,750 --> 00:45:43,958
Sir, the machine is ready
and so is the squadron.

569
00:45:45,125 --> 00:45:46,625
And you yourself said that

570
00:45:46,708 --> 00:45:49,291
we need to bomb them
from outside their missile range,

571
00:45:49,375 --> 00:45:53,041
just like the Mirages.
So we're outside their missile range.

572
00:45:56,041 --> 00:45:57,166
Fair enough.

573
00:45:57,250 --> 00:45:59,500
The army will give you
the coordinates of the peaks.

574
00:45:59,583 --> 00:46:04,125
But how will you calculate
your bomb release point?

575
00:46:04,208 --> 00:46:06,791
Sir, we will conduct our own trials

576
00:46:06,875 --> 00:46:08,333
and create our own charts.

577
00:46:25,916 --> 00:46:26,958
All right.

578
00:46:27,750 --> 00:46:29,666
I will officially

579
00:46:29,750 --> 00:46:32,500
give you clearance
for high-altitude GPS bombing.

580
00:46:34,416 --> 00:46:35,291
But…

581
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:38,500
the error rate of your trials

582
00:46:38,583 --> 00:46:40,500
should be within 200 meters.

583
00:46:43,333 --> 00:46:44,333
Sir.

584
00:47:30,875 --> 00:47:34,000
The Army is struggling.
They're losing men every day.

585
00:47:35,416 --> 00:47:38,416
That's why I had
to commit Air Force support,

586
00:47:38,500 --> 00:47:40,083
even while knowing

587
00:47:40,166 --> 00:47:44,250
that the chances of this unconventional
strategy being successful…

588
00:47:45,375 --> 00:47:47,583
is only five percent.

589
00:47:47,666 --> 00:47:51,250
Like every time before,
we don't have another option, sir.

590
00:47:52,625 --> 00:47:54,916
Now either we will create history,

591
00:47:55,833 --> 00:47:57,041
or get buried in it.

592
00:52:07,125 --> 00:52:12,125
Subtitle translation by: Smriti Shalini

